WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.691 --> 00:00:02.371
- [Narrator] The forces of nature remain

00:00:02.371 --> 00:00:05.232
the one thing that man cannot control.

00:00:05.232 --> 00:00:07.710
Despite the comfort our
newfound capabilities

00:00:07.710 --> 00:00:10.188
to predict inclement
weather have afforded us,

00:00:10.188 --> 00:00:11.971
we are reminded time and again that

00:00:11.971 --> 00:00:14.939
there are forces at work
beyond our understanding.

00:00:14.939 --> 00:00:18.059
And as the clouds gather,
we cannot always predict

00:00:18.059 --> 00:00:19.748
what will tumble out of them.

00:00:19.748 --> 00:00:22.210
This October on Friday the 13th,

00:00:22.210 --> 00:00:24.891
from an executive producer
of The Walking Dead

00:00:24.891 --> 00:00:27.440
and an executive producer of The X-Files

00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:29.171
comes six terrifying tales based

00:00:29.171 --> 00:00:31.720
on the podcast phenomenon, Lore.

00:00:31.720 --> 00:00:33.820
Until then, we offer you this short

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.153
film inspired by the series.

00:00:40.559 --> 00:00:42.297
- My name is Rosemarie Sanders.

00:00:42.297 --> 00:00:44.886
I am an earth science teacher.

00:00:44.886 --> 00:00:48.038
So that means I know a thing
or two about the weather.

00:00:48.038 --> 00:00:50.199
Having animals fall from the sky

00:00:50.199 --> 00:00:54.366
has been documented on paper
going back to the 9th century.

00:00:56.438 --> 00:00:57.929
It is disconcerting.

00:00:57.929 --> 00:01:01.727
But some people take it catastrophically.

00:01:01.727 --> 00:01:03.546
- [Narrator] New meaning
was given to the phrase

00:01:03.546 --> 00:01:06.717
raining cats and dogs in June of 2009

00:01:06.717 --> 00:01:08.938
when scattered showers
of frogs rained down

00:01:08.938 --> 00:01:12.815
upon the residents of
Rakoczifalva in Hungary.

00:01:12.815 --> 00:01:15.773
As stunned onlookers
grasped for an explanation,

00:01:15.773 --> 00:01:19.754
the downpour ceased just as
abruptly as it had begun.

00:01:19.754 --> 00:01:23.394
- Sometimes the frogs
have come down alive.

00:01:23.394 --> 00:01:26.525
As they get turned in the
cloud and broken apart,

00:01:26.525 --> 00:01:28.935
sometimes it's pieces of frogs

00:01:28.935 --> 00:01:30.754
and sometimes they're frozen.

00:01:30.754 --> 00:01:34.546
They were pulled very high
into this cumulonimbus cloud.

00:01:34.546 --> 00:01:36.746
It's very cold at the top of the cloud

00:01:36.746 --> 00:01:39.554
and they will freeze and drop suddenly.

00:01:39.554 --> 00:01:41.432
In the heat of the summer,

00:01:41.432 --> 00:01:43.095
you're more prone to have

00:01:43.095 --> 00:01:46.154
this cumulonimbus cloud developing.

00:01:46.154 --> 00:01:49.404
A waterspout can touch down over a pond

00:01:50.517 --> 00:01:54.477
and because frogs are
very lightweight animals,

00:01:54.477 --> 00:01:57.837
they can be pulled into the cloud itself.

00:01:57.837 --> 00:02:00.287
- [Narrator] The same year, a
rainfall of hundreds of fish

00:02:00.287 --> 00:02:02.946
bombarded residents of
Lajamanu, Australia,

00:02:02.946 --> 00:02:06.464
326 miles from the nearest river.

00:02:06.464 --> 00:02:09.265
Even today, the scientific
community has yet to reach

00:02:09.265 --> 00:02:12.465
consensus on an explanation
for the phenomenon.

00:02:12.465 --> 00:02:16.202
- Honestly, it would depend
on the size of the animal.

00:02:16.202 --> 00:02:20.796
It would also depend on the
strength of the system itself.

00:02:20.796 --> 00:02:23.745
And it can fall great distance
from where it was first

00:02:23.745 --> 00:02:26.916
picked up because the
cloud would be traveling.

00:02:26.916 --> 00:02:30.254
When you see in reports in the mid-west,

00:02:30.254 --> 00:02:33.345
you can get softball-sized hail stones.

00:02:33.345 --> 00:02:36.564
They weigh a lot more than a frog.

00:02:36.564 --> 00:02:41.124
Now a lot of times frogs or
fish raining from the sky

00:02:41.124 --> 00:02:43.791
is often seen as a sign from God

00:02:44.644 --> 00:02:47.884
or an upset of the natural world.

00:02:47.884 --> 00:02:49.295
- [Narrator] The Old Testament is filled

00:02:49.295 --> 00:02:52.073
with such examples of
a vengeful God's wrath.

00:02:52.073 --> 00:02:54.633
In the book of Exodus, a
plague of frogs rained down

00:02:54.633 --> 00:02:56.684
upon the people of Egypt as punishment

00:02:56.684 --> 00:02:59.644
for Pharaoh's refusal
to free the Israelites.

00:02:59.644 --> 00:03:02.353
Are the raining animals an
environmental disruption

00:03:02.353 --> 00:03:04.905
to be explained by
further scientific study

00:03:04.905 --> 00:03:06.854
or are these modern day plagues,

00:03:06.854 --> 00:03:09.660
a warning that the end of days is near?

00:03:09.660 --> 00:03:13.752
- It can be frogs, it can
be fish and it can be birds.

00:03:13.752 --> 00:03:17.919
And any anomaly in the natural
world can be very disruptive.

00:03:19.402 --> 00:03:20.665
Without sounding trite,

00:03:20.665 --> 00:03:22.998
I would say watch your step.

